EvoBuddy @VERSION@ (linux-@ARCH@)
=================================

A UI study build: the interface of a desktop client, reproduced natively in
GTK 3. Wording and icons are placeholders; no brand assets are reproduced.

Self-contained
--------------
This bundle carries GTK 3 and every library it needs, its own fonts, its icon
theme and its compiled GSettings schemas. It wants glibc >= 2.28, an X display
and nothing else — no GTK, no fontconfig and no fonts of any kind need to be
installed. The libraries still taken from the host are glibc's own, on purpose:
they are forward compatible, and bundling libc breaks name resolution.

It was verified by running exactly this tree on a machine with none of the
above, which is the only way that claim means anything.

Run
---
    ./run

Install for the current user (launcher on PATH + menu entry):

    ./install.sh              # under ~/.local
    ./install.sh /some/prefix

Known gaps
----------
CJK input goes through XIM: the bundle has GTK's input-method modules, but not
ibus's, which ships separately.
